\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. In the bleak mid-winter,
\par Frosty wind made moan,
\par Earth stood hard as iron,
\par Water like a stone;
\par Snow had fallen, snow on snow,
\par Snow on snow,
\par In the bleak mid-winter,
\par Long ago.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Our God, heaven cannot hold Him,
\par Nor earth sustain;
\par Heaven and earth shall flee away
\par When He comes to reign;
\par In the bleak mid-winter,
\par A stable-place sufficed
\par The Lord God Almighty,
\par Jesus Christ.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Angels and archangels
\par May have gathered there,
\par Cherubim and seraphim
\par Thronged the air;
\par But His mother only,
\par In her maiden bliss,
\par Worshipped the beloved with a kiss.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. What can I give Him,
\par Poor as I am
\par If I were a shepherd,
\par I would  bring a lamb;
\par If I were a wise man,
\par I would do my part;
\par Yet what I can I give Him-
\par Give my heart.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2 
\par }

